{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"frangible-even-quahog","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nBug 4dd1-7963-e15e-4e2c fixed the compaction sweep running unbounded git history walks inside the store write lock for signed events its --no-merges position map misses. How often the production server hits that path is unmeasured.\n\n## Approach\nRead-only, on the MCP server's tickets clone via SSM: count signed events whose only adding commit is a merge commit, on a COPY or with a bounded git invocation, never mutating the live store.\n\n## Testing\nRead-only command output recorded on the ticket; no code change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The count of merge-only signed events in the server clone is recorded with the command used and its timestamp (checked: ticket comment).\n","id":"08c8-6262-3f5a-4110","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["tracker","compaction","verification"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Measure how often the production compaction sweep misses the position map"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792908638120595001,"uuid":"9ee1a7a0-4080-4c4d-abe1-20e11a064783"}